{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014jJdvHkBoufLwzG21L4Vtq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# docs/orphans-allow — the meta-repo's EXPECTED live-orphan census (WI-228).\n2\t#\n3\t# Read by project-trajectory/scripts/check_docs.py. A \"live orphan\" is a doc no\n4\t# navigation path reaches from an entry root. Most of ours are RETAINED EVIDENCE\n5\t# — round reviews, closed-WI specs, dual-plan artifacts, generated indexes — that\n6\t# must stay on disk yet is not a navigation node: \"unlinked-from-navigation\" is\n7\t# the wrong frame for it. Each non-comment line is a shell glob (fnmatch, repo-\n8\t# relative POSIX; `*` spans separators, so `docs/reviews/*` covers the whole\n9\t# subtree). A matched orphan is EXPECTED — dropped from the per-doc warnings, an\n10\t# aggregate `note` in their place, and never a finding (even under\n11\t# --strict-orphans). An orphan matching NOTHING here is GENUINE: it warns (fails\n12\t# under --strict-orphans), the newly-introduced-orphan RATCHET — link/index it,\n13\t# or, if it is a new evidence class, add its glob here with a reason.\n14\t#\n15\t# WHY a census, not deletion-or-mass-indexing (repo-review-2026-07-18 M-07):\n16\t# deleting would destroy history; indexing everything would bloat navigation\n17\t# (status.md / README stay lean). This bounds the noise so a genuinely\n18\t# undiscoverable new doc no longer hides in 60-odd steady warnings — the same\n19\t# silent-growth mode docs/dupes-allow bounds for duplication and the C901\n20\t# ratchet (WI-225) bounds for complexity. A GENUINE straggler is linked instead\n21\t# of listed: docs/specs/parallel-dispatch-design-notes.md is reached from its\n22\t# companion plan, so it is navigable and absent below.\n23\t\n24\t# review evidence — the per-round Reviewer/Critique/Grounding artifacts and the\n25\t# top-level whole-repo reviews; kept as the audit trail, referenced from log.md.\n26\tdocs/reviews/*\n27\tdocs/repo-review-*.md\n28\t\n29\t