eport.md\",\n+            \"--strict-orphans\",\n+        ],\n+        cwd=ROOT,\n+    )\n+    assert proc.returncode == 0, proc.stdout + proc.stderr\n+    # No genuine orphan is ever named as a finding (WARN or FAIL) on the meta tree.\n+    assert \"orphan doc (no path from an entry root)\" not in proc.stdout\n+    # ... and the census is non-empty: the classified evidence is folded into the\n+    # aggregate note, proving suppression is actually happening (not vacuously 0).\n+    assert \"expected live-orphan(s) matched docs/orphans-allow\" in proc.stdout","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"168ca743-b860-429f-b049-593539a315ed","uuid":"122a60e4-4891-4da2-96be-96e0c89aa99c","timestamp":"2026-07-18T22:51:32.534Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/docs/specs/WI-228.md b/docs/specs/WI-228.md\nindex 99f15d4..dda4dd9 100644\n--- a/docs/specs/WI-228.md\n+++ b/docs/specs/WI-228.md\n@@ -5,17 +5,20 @@\n \n ## Why\n \n-`check_docs` reports 48 live orphan warnings. Most are *retained evidence* —\n-reviews, closed-WI specs, plan-round artifacts — that should stay live but\n-unlinked-from-navigation is the wrong frame for them; meanwhile genuinely\n-undiscoverable new docs hide in the same noise. Deleting or globally\n-ignoring would destroy history; indexing everything would bloat navigation\n-(§0 table). The census only ever grows silently — the same failure mode\n-WI-225 ratchets for complexity.\n+`check_docs` reports dozens of live orphan warnings — measured **63** on the\n+integration tree at filing (2026-07-18); it was 48 when this WI was first\n+drafted on `dualplan-routing-fix`, and the drift is the point: the census is a\n+*moving target by construction*, so no fixed count belongs in the acceptance\n+criterion (see Done-when). Most are *retained evidence* — reviews, closed-WI\n+specs, plan-round artifacts — that should stay live but unlinked-from-navigation\n+is the wrong frame for them; meanwhile genuinely undiscoverable new docs hide 