{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdALrWqf321EGSaqNKqE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The trailers are present and the tree is clean. WI-228's REVIEW-A rework is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**REVIEW-A finding (MINOR, CHANGES-REQUESTED):** the WI-228 spec pinned a hardcoded \"48\" live-orphan baseline that was untraceable — the checker actually measures **63** over the integration tree, and the count is a moving target *by construction* (it was 48 when the spec was drafted on `dualplan-routing-fix`). That fragility is the exact silent-growth failure mode the WI ratchets against.\n\n**Fix — took the \"make the criterion count-independent\" path (the reviewer's second option), plus recorded the measured census for traceability:**\n\n1. **Spec amendment** (`docs/specs/WI-228.md`, Why/Scope/Done-when):\n   - Records the measured **63-item census** as an as-of snapshot (48 at draft → 63 at integration), explaining *why* the drift is expected.\n   - Rewrites Done-when so the acceptance criterion is explicitly **count-independent**: the invariant is \"every live orphan classified — zero unexplained residue,\" not any fixed number.\n\n2. **Regression assertion** (`tests/test_check_docs.py::test_meta_repo_has_zero_unexplained_orphans`):\n   - Runs `check_docs` against the **real meta root** under `--strict-orphans` (matching the harness `--ignore` for the generated trace composite) and requires exit 0 — dogfooding the ratchet on the kit's own tree, following the existing `test_derive_gate.py` meta-dogfood precedent.\n   - Asserts the *invariant*, not a number: no genuine-orphan finding, and the aggregate note proves suppression is actually happening (census non-empty, not vacuously 0). It goes red the moment an unclassified orphan lands, whatever the count is.\n\n**Verification:**\n- ruff format `--check` + lint: clean\n- Smoke tier (per-commit bar): **853 passed, 2 skipped**\n- Full unfiltered suite 